# Line endings, and why the bundled data is exempt from them.
#
# Source and documentation are normalised to LF inside the repository and
# checked out in whatever style the platform prefers. That is the usual
# arrangement and it is fine for code.
#
# The files under tvtt/data are a different matter. Every transcription has a
# SHA-256 recorded in sources.json, and "tvtt verify" compares the bytes on
# disk against it. If Git rewrote their line endings on checkout, eight of the
# nine would hash differently on Windows and verify would report the bundled
# data as corrupt -- on a clean clone, with nothing actually wrong. The same
# bytes also have to reach every platform for a run to be reproducible.
#
# So: no conversion, ever, for anything shipped as data.

* text=auto

tvtt/data/** -text
*.ttf binary
